---
/**
 * The page. It prints what the state says and nothing else.
 *
 * **Every number on this page was read out of a repository by a machine.** There is no
 * hard-coded stage, role, test count, phase or commit here, and there is a test that
 * holds this true: the state is a separate file written by `scripts/ask_the_family.mjs`,
 * and a fact that is not in that file cannot appear here.
 *
 * **This page is about four repositories rather than one**, and that changes what the
 * first rule has to survive. The page it is a view of refuses to print a section it
 * could not read; here one project failing to answer must not take the other three off
 * the page. So the rule has a second half: **a project is read, or the page says in
 * words that it could not be.**
 *
 * **What is written by hand is only what the repositories cannot refute**: the pitch,
 * and who to write to. A number somebody typed is a number that goes stale quietly.
 */
---
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>ai-sdlc — four repositories, one domain</title>
		<style>
			@import "tailwindcss";
		</style>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-[#fafaf9] text-zinc-900 antialiased">
		<main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16"></main>
	</body>
</html>
